    challengesLabel: THE CHALLENGES
    challenge: <p data-start="196" data-end="471"><strong data-start="196" data-end="232">Transport order management — TMS</strong><br data-start="232" data-end="235">Without a centralized TMS, transport orders come in by email, phone, and WhatsApp. Assignments are managed in spreadsheets, confirmations are sent as PDFs, and disputes are impossible to trace. Every shipment becomes a manual operation.</p><p data-start="473" data-end="709"><strong data-start="473" data-end="501">Route planning &amp; loading</strong><br data-start="501" data-end="504">Optimizing loads, assigning the right vehicles and drivers, and respecting customer delivery windows — without a dedicated tool, this work takes hours every morning and generates avoidable transport costs.</p><p data-start="711" data-end="938"><strong data-start="711" data-end="743">Fleet tracking &amp; maintenance</strong><br data-start="743" data-end="746">Mileage is recorded in notebooks, maintenance checks are forgotten, and breakdowns immobilize vehicles without warning. Without centralized tracking, fleet costs quickly become uncontrollable.</p><p data-start="940" data-end="1163"><strong data-start="940" data-end="973">Transport invoicing &amp; pricing</strong><br data-start="973" data-end="976">Invoicing based on weight, volume, distance, pricing zones, or each customer’s specific conditions — without a dedicated tool — is a constant source of errors and silently erodes margins.</p><p data-start="1165" data-end="1379"><strong data-start="1165" data-end="1205">Transport documents &amp; CMR compliance</strong><br data-start="1205" data-end="1208">Managing CMRs, delivery notes, and customs certificates on paper exposes the company to costly disputes. Digitalization has become both an operational and legal necessity.</p>
